feat(coordination): pd done refuses unpushed branches + requires PR url in result

Hard precondition for `pd done`: refuse to mark a session complete unless
the branch is fully pushed to origin AND the result note carries one of
three sentinels (PR URL, no-pr-yet:, not-applicable:). Escape hatch:
--skip-origin-check --reason "<reason>" stamps [OPERATOR-OVERRIDE] into
the note for auditability.

Motivated by the 2026-05-20 incident where 9 worktree branches were
orphaned because agents wrote pd done without ever pushing.

Implementation:
- lib/git-origin-check.ts (NEW): execFileSync-based check of
  rev-list @{u}..HEAD --count plus PR-URL / sentinel regexes.
- lib/sugar.ts: precondition gate in done() applied only for
  status=completed; abandoned sessions pass through unchanged.
- routes/sugar.ts: new HTTP 400 codes for the refusals.
- cli/commands/sugar.ts: --skip-origin-check + --reason flags,
  prints the structured hint indented under the error.
- lib/client.ts (DoneSugarOptions): new skipOriginCheck fields.
- lib/spawner.ts: spawner-managed agents auto-bypass with reason
  (subprocess lifecycle, not feature-branch lifecycle).

Tests:
- 5 new unit cases in tests/unit/sugar.test.js exercising the gate
  via an injected gitOriginChecker stub.
- Existing unit tests + integration tests updated to either include
  a sentinel in their note or use the documented escape hatch.

Validation:
- 202 unit suites pass (5810 tests).
- tsc --noEmit clean.


